<section id='individual-reflection-introduction'>
    <p>
        This individual reflection is intended to help respondents identify the areas of Digital Fluency that they might find useful for their roles. Recommendations will be generated upon completion. Users are encouraged to review and explore the Digital Fluency training options within the Training Portal.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you would like to review the college’s Digital Fluency Framework before beginning this questionnaire, please visit <a href="https://example.com/digital-fluency" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the college's Digital Fluency Website (opens in a new tab)</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        Questions and feedback about the questionnaire can be directed by email to <a href="mailto:digitalfluency@example.com">digitalfluency@example.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        The college's DF Framework includes 4 Indicators demonstrated through 3 levels of ability:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Competent:</strong> User’s digital skills are foundational and the person demonstrates basic functionality and abilities to engage in the behaviours, skills, and mindsets outlined in the Indicator.</li>
        <li><strong>Proficient:</strong> User demonstrates mid-level capabilities outlined in the Indicator.</li>
        <li><strong>Leader:</strong> User demonstrates advanced capabilities, encourages others to advance and/or is participating in larger-scale institutional efforts that align with the Indicator.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The following sections are divided into the 4 Indicators. Answer each question to determine your familiarity with and/or interest in the topic. Additional questions may appear to assess your desired level of ability. 
    </p>
    <p>
        Finally, click <strong>Download Recommendations</strong> to download your recommended courses.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note:</strong> This questionnaire is completely private and no identifying information is captured. 
    </p>
</section>